[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-62051"] :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 4+4\\times 6 \\\\  & =8+24 \\\\  & =32\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248/selection/c7185865339a97ca9d3349f5fc2c313837534dc8b9bb95953e40ca6b42cee427" :answer/id #uuid "feec887f-d0eb-56d9-8906-0efc8097c725" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$782$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248/selection/c79f46ddf91f78779b85fd9ace446efa12b12c14885e99b95d05b5418037424b" :answer/id #uuid "225e1086-5a1b-5246-ac5e-a62929728648" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$827$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248/selection/18a5fc47c71b7da482845d2c9f01649038ec7d1c3698ef230f72de929a8d4432" :answer/id #uuid "8eed53d2-4cb0-5293-b007-12540aad1a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$728$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248/selection/26cfdb3393adfd8afb5a707d44ffab1ac1563a6b7aa1e7d775af77003f9eecf9" :answer/id #uuid "d941a6d5-c450-5474-a23a-d9d374030b08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$211$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248/selection/e8d61926dec9a70df1fb25b8c0f31d0fff939bb5fb3320d7015a29fe5d7738cb" :answer/id #uuid "2dc158a0-96ab-512d-847b-7ca73f08ca86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$112$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75904f92-8b53-52a8-9ce0-04342c711241" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-62248/selection/18a5fc47c71b7da482845d2c9f01649038ec7d1c3698ef230f72de929a8d4432" :answer-field/choices ["q-62248/selection/c7185865339a97ca9d3349f5fc2c313837534dc8b9bb95953e40ca6b42cee427" "q-62248/selection/c79f46ddf91f78779b85fd9ace446efa12b12c14885e99b95d05b5418037424b" "q-62248/selection/18a5fc47c71b7da482845d2c9f01649038ec7d1c3698ef230f72de929a8d4432" "q-62248/selection/26cfdb3393adfd8afb5a707d44ffab1ac1563a6b7aa1e7d775af77003f9eecf9" "q-62248/selection/e8d61926dec9a70df1fb25b8c0f31d0fff939bb5fb3320d7015a29fe5d7738cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-62248" :question/id #uuid "abe6fddf-a313-54f2-92c6-9b51675460f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-62248" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/c241f6afc3978dfc8d1e2a048509a2e6fc7c91b0caf5ac4814a864edc3992d0c.png)\n\nChloe wants to paint a steel box that has the form of a rectangular prism. Two of the polygonal faces are $4\\,\\text{ft}\\times 4\\,\\text{ft}$ squares. If the cost to paint the surface is $$6.50$ per square foot, how much will it cost her in total? Note that Chloe does *not* need to paint the square sides." :question/worked-solution "The net of our prism is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/7b84a48933abb96f605476c6d703406227b0fe5301b1457a447cdbb3f58f0937.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nEach side face (apart from the square faces) of our solid is a rectangle, where the base is $7\\,\\text{ft}$ and the height is $4\\,\\text{ft}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=7\\times 4=28\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, the total area of the side surfaces consists of $4$ rectangular faces. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area of the sides} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle}) \\\\  & =4\\times 28 \\\\  & =112\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the cost to paint the surface is $$6.50$ per square foot, the total amount that Chloe will have to pay is\n\n$$\n112\\times 6.50=$728.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-62248/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-62248"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-62256"] :question/worked-solution "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/09eff98ca31b4bb350e2d793dcfa6e6972de25bb3b613c898533068c36fe9a78.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $2\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=2\\times 2=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $2\\,\\text{m}$ and the height is $9\\,\\text{m}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 2\\times 9=9\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =4+4\\times 9 \\\\  & =4+36 \\\\  & =40\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339/selection/b8a3531e06322c287d7144dc334e828cff1fe8c4c4aee93e5089ad9ebf623da6" :answer/id #uuid "003a7090-fd03-5d1d-b08b-fea6622268b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "274\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339/selection/da845eec756467240f744893afba14a0d0716a6b7c912d7716851d00703364d3" :answer/id #uuid "cf89489f-8249-5812-962c-2d0f5ea5bd86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "264\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339/selection/aab8fabf76cbc1a699bb2f14b2b628109e54f3e74b00f8a2c0a630b3597c1854" :answer/id #uuid "08a5a31b-a83b-516d-966d-64b1029c4491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "286\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339/selection/d186fe0adf623c2cb966e52dbd40c7db8d4b18d669695dfc83cd0cd5f8520b35" :answer/id #uuid "9affc390-41f3-5c35-a577-4c936322fb7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339/selection/a52c1628084afcb3a3a7ddb4e9aa62454896de49840f78e57f629b99b5a944e4" :answer/id #uuid "aa04db1a-e99c-5749-94e6-88155a2e98bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "302\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bfbea19-b364-52b6-a407-de820d1e178f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93339/selection/d186fe0adf623c2cb966e52dbd40c7db8d4b18d669695dfc83cd0cd5f8520b35" :answer-field/choices ["q-93339/selection/b8a3531e06322c287d7144dc334e828cff1fe8c4c4aee93e5089ad9ebf623da6" "q-93339/selection/da845eec756467240f744893afba14a0d0716a6b7c912d7716851d00703364d3" "q-93339/selection/aab8fabf76cbc1a699bb2f14b2b628109e54f3e74b00f8a2c0a630b3597c1854" "q-93339/selection/d186fe0adf623c2cb966e52dbd40c7db8d4b18d669695dfc83cd0cd5f8520b35" "q-93339/selection/a52c1628084afcb3a3a7ddb4e9aa62454896de49840f78e57f629b99b5a944e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93339" :question/id #uuid "e4c5c8b2-a316-5095-80a5-7c0b82a638cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-93339" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/a60731e7df54bb8f18f834b818c3e49c79fb30e67f7ed50c40f40aa813689ece.png)\n\nA manufacturer produces an unfair tetrahedral die from a plastic net, shown above. What is the total surface area of the die?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ base triangle and $3$ side triangles. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 64+3\\times 78 \\\\  & =64+234 \\\\  & =298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93339/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208/selection/e06201847481719cab9335b10f0d8465879e21994c1aebad8ea66cd1bf38737b" :answer/id #uuid "cd2f358e-d060-5361-9e36-0857128bf9e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "148\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208/selection/207c0d953d8bcb7222d1d3c136d782a6399a4ff1a89378163e867446ed493e8f" :answer/id #uuid "3bb38e1a-94a3-5217-aca2-aab60076c4b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "144\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208/selection/0a37501bd5a3cdbd35a0c3bacde7f1d7749ed1190c8ade56bc3451d31c0f5e00" :answer/id #uuid "3e07cb84-d0b4-5170-bb6d-8e0aff34a673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208/selection/2b3b12594e8fc6d30ff553662d8d3407afd6d654579dce010f4da143e23f54dd" :answer/id #uuid "58ef7413-d232-53e3-b05b-cc4e25c64794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "164\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208/selection/30afde64b9ea6d779cf1d600162dcc408604a27cbe15ae1101df6ab324aadafa" :answer/id #uuid "858d11dc-8943-5927-9a54-8f1821d56261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "156\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "567812c0-b06b-53d3-a732-67726c6b5fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119208/selection/30afde64b9ea6d779cf1d600162dcc408604a27cbe15ae1101df6ab324aadafa" :answer-field/choices ["q-119208/selection/e06201847481719cab9335b10f0d8465879e21994c1aebad8ea66cd1bf38737b" "q-119208/selection/207c0d953d8bcb7222d1d3c136d782a6399a4ff1a89378163e867446ed493e8f" "q-119208/selection/0a37501bd5a3cdbd35a0c3bacde7f1d7749ed1190c8ade56bc3451d31c0f5e00" "q-119208/selection/2b3b12594e8fc6d30ff553662d8d3407afd6d654579dce010f4da143e23f54dd" "q-119208/selection/30afde64b9ea6d779cf1d600162dcc408604a27cbe15ae1101df6ab324aadafa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119208" :question/id #uuid "8020cab4-3d7d-5a11-9426-5c8de74166ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-119208" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/4f2807a0989a3f36376d1ed93d02162ded72200803d28b49caab701176837628.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular pyramid represented by the net above?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 36+4\\times 30 \\\\  & =36+120 \\\\  & =156\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119208/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119208"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
